{"type":"assistant-stream","frame":{"type":"chunk","attemptId":"session-83d91d7a-759a-4689-80ef-d600f436f80a:1","revision":611,"index":609,"time":1793864956025,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user wants two independent tasks done in parallel:\n1. Write \"今日待办\" (today's todos) into todo.md\n2. Calculate the sum 1+2+...+100 and write the calculation process into sum.txt\n\nBoth tasks involve creating files, so per my instructions, I should delegate them to worker bots via create_bot. Since the tasks are independent, I can create two workers concurrently in one message.\n\nWait — \"今日待办\" — what content should go into todo.md? The user just says \"把「今日待办」写进 todo.md\" — write \"今日待办\" into todo.md. This is ambiguous: it could mean write the literal text \"今日待办\" as a header, or write today's todo list. Actually, reading it literally, it seems they want the text \"今日待办\" written into todo.md. That's simple enough — a title. Perhaps a todo.md with a \"今日待办\" heading. I shouldn't over-interpret. The simplest interpretation: create todo.md containing \"今日待办\" (maybe as a markdown heading). I'll have the worker write \"# 今日待办\" as the content. Actually to be safe, just write the literal text \"今日待办\" into the file. The user said 把「今日待办」写进 todo.md — write \"今日待办\" into todo.md. So the content is exactly 今日待办. I'll instruct the worker to write that literal text.\n\nThe sum task: 1+2+...+100 = 5050, using Gauss's method: (1+100)*100/2 = 5050. Write the calculation process into sum.txt.\n\nThese are trivial file writes but per the system prompt, any request that creates or changes files belongs in a worker via create_bot. Two independent tasks → two workers created concurrently.\n\nLet me create both workers in one message with two create_bot calls."}}}}
{"type":"assistant-stream","frame":{"type":"chunk","attemptId":"session-83d91d7a-759a-4689-80ef-d600f436f80a:1","revision":612,"index":610,"time":1793864956026,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"text","text":"这两件事相互独立，我会同时启动两个工作线程分别处理：一个把「今日待办」写入 todo.md，另一个计算 1 加到 100 并把过程写入 sum.txt。"}}}}
